    "rich_text_YDRt3G": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_EHgdj6": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "5 Key Benefits of Foil Tape",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_L6CVqK": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Foil tape provides a number of advantages for critical industries and applications. Here are five of the primary benefits offered by foil tape:</p><p> </p><ul><li><strong>Extreme cold and heat resistance. </strong>Foil tape with any metal presents a high level of temperature versatility. Our extensive selection of foil tapes can withstand temperatures from -22°F to 248°F and can be applied to products in temperatures from 14°F to 104°F. Unlike traditional adhesive tapes that will harden and perform poorly in cold temperatures, foil tapes retain adhesion even in freezing temperatures.</li><li><strong>Extended service life. </strong>Our foil tapes are manufactured using state-of-the-art acrylic adhesive technology, which offers exceptional cohesion, adhesion, and thermal stability. Foil tapes perform better over time compared with standard rubber adhesives, making them ideal for limited access applications where replacement is difficult, such as insulation or drainage layers in new construction.</li><li><strong>Moisture resistance. </strong>The moisture resistance of foil tapes makes them well suited to use in the marine industry, where they can be applied to patching without becoming waterlogged or losing adhesion. The moisture resistance of foil tapes is so superior that Scientific American once suggested it could be used to manufacture a boat that could carry cargo.</li><li><strong>Resistant to harsh chemicals. </strong>Foil tape is especially resistant to harsh chemicals, which makes it ideal in extreme conditions where saltwater, oil, fuel, and corrosive chemicals are found. For this reason, it is often employed by the Navy to protect wheels, windows, and seams during paint stripping. It is also used to seal equipment used for anodizing and electroplating applications.</li><li><strong>Recyclable</strong>. Aluminum foil tape is recyclable and requires only 5% of the energy needed for its initial production for recycling. This makes it one of the most sustainable adhesive tape materials on the market.</li></ul>",
            "text_size": "text-base",
            "text_line_limit": "none",
            "button_style": "btn--underline",
            "button_icon": "none"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_EHgdj6",
        "text_L6CVqK"
      ],
